{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IN:title", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Cohen-Macaulay schemes", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-Cohen-Macaulay}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:ce7f499b4297964b630d65594c1c5d74f2ee80ddd917cd4044dbe80f0574550f", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:076c02da61d8d874bc190edd48a3fea41fb74d3e4c7fa51fedfcbbc06fcc1e42", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IN:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall, see Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>,\nthat a local Noetherian ring <MATH_0001> is\nsaid to be Cohen-Macaulay if <MATH_0002>.\nRecall that a Noetherian ring <MATH_0003> is said to be Cohen-Macaulay if\nevery local ring <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> is Cohen-Macaulay,\nsee Algebra, Definition <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-local-ring-CM}", "MATH_0001": "$(R, \\mathfrak m)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{depth}_{\\mathfrak m}(R) = \\dim(R)$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$R_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-definition-ring-CM}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:1979d9ce23bcb3d93c771a87aaacfceaa415697917527ecdbf3d467144be0582", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:afcd554f547d9661c3aac64d68cf14c78f6e91085e62e7eda93bc4bd94ecd12d", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09dd0c9f21569a12e9549004fa7b658487039f0a69d4c6db437db6e97f0824a9"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IO:statement", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Cohen-Macaulay<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\nfor every <MATH_0003> there exists an affine open neighbourhood\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> such that the ring <MATH_0006> is\nNoetherian and Cohen-Macaulay.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-Cohen-Macaulay}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:e4236a1cdf28cfc244f330f9999d7dcea5d7b4eba400100bdae479bcf14768fc", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6316364c36117e69c9cbe5025ac1bf6da3f5f3e56b8dda0fb9d64598c13ac0c", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0b2eb5d6445e3fef7cf6e8525ac32f2f97d358fa8fbe445912adb428a19a6525"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IP:statement", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is Cohen-Macaulay,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally Noetherian and all of its local rings are Cohen-Macaulay,\nand\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0004> is locally Noetherian and for any closed point <MATH_0005>\nthe local ring <MATH_0006> is Cohen-Macaulay.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-Cohen-Macaulay}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:a4414ebd22bf2ca611ad23c262c14e0af02c9fabbeaf1a5db07d91475b00f322", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:31c84565c4a28da080880cf6efa106f42787ae72a276c2f4595b93bbc4e187ec", "source_math_hash": "sha256:066224f805a8414e8226d8a586a98bd42d64eab462af5b3b407ed490c33091a7"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IP:proof", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Algebra, Lemma <REF_0001> says that the localization of\na Cohen-Macaulay local ring is Cohen-Macaulay. The lemma follows\nby combining this with Lemma <REF_0002>,\nwith the existence of closed\npoints on locally Noetherian schemes\n(Lemma <REF_0003>), and\nthe definitions.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-localize-CM}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-Noetherian-closed-point}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:4227b2955013f6c8b191a51e71a0ceff69838715f83993f67998658403202cab", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e00698bcdc5fb6930f751711bc05a5adcaa666645d96ef70b46f2dc6cd239cac", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:02IQ:statement", "parent_tag": "02IN", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is Cohen-Macaulay.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis Noetherian and Cohen-Macaulay.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is Noetherian and Cohen-Macaulay.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is Cohen-Macaulay.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is Cohen-Macaulay then every open subscheme\nis Cohen-Macaulay.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0009": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-Cohen-Macaulay}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a1d3feb82a698e5badbbdf1950962635215d43a3a8c9fb25d209900e86418fb", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:97b6ba5cd90488db7a8bb82eacdc46a1429b36c570ef26b333f854c1e0b04394", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24"}
